user_prompt:
Please conduct a thematic analysis of the following interview data.

QUANTITATIVE GROUNDING:
- Total respondents: 18 (9 transit_primary, 9 car_primary)
- Average response length: ~114 characters, ~20 words per response
- Top words transit cohort: app, when, miss, train, delays
- Top words car cohort: when, drive, transit, parking, time
- Theme frequencies (UX mentions: transit=10, car=7; Trust mentions: transit=4, car=2; 
  Safety mentions: transit=2, car=2; Pain mentions: transit=5, car=3)

INTERVIEW DATA:
[
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-01",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "The live arrival board is what I open first; when it is wrong I miss connections and the rest of my day slides sideways."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-02",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "Crowding is my main pain\u2014sometimes I skip a train even if the app says it is on time because I know the platform will be unsafe."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-03",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "Pricing feels opaque; I want a single place that shows weekly caps and discounts without digging through three menus."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-04",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "Night service gaps are scary; the app should pair walking directions with the last train so I am not guessing alone at midnight."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-05",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "Accessibility info is hit or miss\u2014elevator outages are buried; I need that louder than marketing banners."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-06",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "I appreciate offline mode when tunnels drop signal; that single feature keeps me from switching apps."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-07",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "Transfers are where the UX fails: same station but different names across lines and the map does not reconcile them."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-08",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "Delays are fine if the explanation is honest\u2014generic delays erode trust faster than a long wait with a reason."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-09",
    "cohort": "transit_primary",
    "response": "I wish the app surfaced bike-share docks near the exit I actually use; routing assumes a generic street corner."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-10",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "I drive when transit is unreliable; the app\u2019s drive-time estimate helps me decide but parking costs are never in the same view."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-11",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "Traffic alerts are useful but noisy; I only want reroutes when the delay exceeds what I would lose searching for parking."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-12",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "I combine park-and-ride; the app should stitch driving legs with train legs instead of treating them as separate trips."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-13",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "Safety at the lot matters more than saving two minutes; I want lighting and CCTV notes not just cheapest price."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-14",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "Carpool matching is gimmicky unless it respects my fixed drop-off time; otherwise I ignore those prompts."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-15",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "Fuel vs fare comparison would help families like mine decide weekly; right now it is guesswork across spreadsheets."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-16",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "The interface is crowded; I only need three buttons on the home screen and everything else feels like clutter."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-17",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "When transit is on strike I need a single banner that explains alternatives\u2014not a feed of unrelated news."
  },
  {
    "respondent_id": "INT-18",
    "cohort": "car_primary",
    "response": "I trust the map more than the ETA; if the line on the map is wrong I assume the whole trip plan is wrong."
  }
]

Please provide a comprehensive thematic analysis.
